Inclusion Criteria:
  - Adult patients [AND] who plan to undergo simultaneous primary total knee arthroplasty on bilateral knee joint [AND] with a diagnosis of osteoarthritis [OR] aseptic bone necrosis, [BUT] [NOT] rheumatoid arthritis;
  - All patients [AND] who have normal preoperative platelet count, [AND] normal prothrombin time, [AND] normal partial thromboplastin time, [AND] normal international normalized ratio;
  - The use of only balanced electrolyte solutions [OR] albumin for plasma volume restitution.
Exclusion Criteria:
  - Allergy to tranexamic acid;
  - Receiving warfarin [OR] heparin; [OR] had a history of hemophilia, deep venous thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, [OR] renal impairment; [OR] [OR] were pregnant;
  - Patients with any cardiovascular problems (such as myocardiac infarction history, atrial fibrillation, angina);
  - Patients with thromboembolic disorders, [OR] those exhibiting a deteriorating general condition;
  - Preoperative anemia (a hemoglobin value of <11 g/dL in females [AND] <12 g/dL in males), [AND] refusal of blood products;
  - Preoperative use of anticoagulant therapy within five days before surgery, fibrinolytic disorders requiring intraoperative antifibrinolytic treatment, coagulopathy (as identified by a preoperative platelet count of <150,000/mm3, [AND] an international normalized ratio of >1.4, [OR] [OR] a prolonged partial thromboplastin time [>1.4 times normal]).
