  2. Clinically judged patients with p0~pIV initial treatment.（1 Variable risk factors are overeating food (habits) [AND] family history. 2 Among all the patients, the ratio of male to female is 3:1, [AND] the age is between 50 [AND] 70 years old. [OR] In addition to eating too hot food, other eating habits (such as eating fresh fruits [AND] vegetables, eating preserved food, etc.) are consistent, other factors (such as BMI, smoking, drinking, etc.) as much as possible. 3 In order to rule out the interference of other diseases, each sample needs to be determined to have [NOT] history of other diseases (such as neurodegenerative diseases, leukemia).）
  3. The normal population comes from the healthy population of Nanfang Hospital Health Center of Southern Medical University.
Exclusion Criteria:
  1. Preoperative patients have received relevant treatment, such as radiotherapy [OR] chemotherapy;
  2. The subject has other diseases, such as tumors in other parts;
  3. Patients [NOT] meet the age;
  4. There is [NOT] guarantee that other eating habits (such as eating fresh fruits [AND] vegetables, [NOT] eating preserved foods) [AND] other factors (such as BMI, smoking, drinking, etc.) are basically the same.
