Inclusion Criteria:
  1. Participants [AND] will be adults [AND] who utilize English as their primary language.
  2. Unilateral severe [OR] profound sensorineural hearing loss for a duration of at least 6 months (to ensure stability of hearing loss), [BUT] [NOT] greater than 10 years.
  3. Contralateral ear with normal, [OR] near-normal, hearing.
  4. Poorer ear (ear to be implanted): severe [OR] profound sensorineural hearing loss, defined as pure-tone thresholds 70 dB HL [OR] greater for the frequencies 500, 1000,
     2000, 3000, [AND] 4000 Hz with monosyllabic word understanding, as measured using the CNC Word Test at 60 dBA under earphones, less than [OR] equal to 20%
  5. Better ear (contralateral ear): normal [OR] near-normal hearing defined as pure-tone thresholds [NOT] poorer than 30 dB HL at 250, 500, 1000, 2000, [AND] 3000 Hz [AND] [NOT] poorer than 40 dB HL at 4000 Hz with monosyllabic word understanding, as measured using the CNC Word Test at 60 dBA under earphones, of greater than [OR] equal to 85%.
  6. Willingness to comply with all study requirements.
  7. Patent cochlea [AND] normal cochlear anatomy.
Exclusion Criteria:
  1. Medical [OR] psychological conditions that contraindicate undergoing surgery.
  2. Ossification [OR] any other cochlear anomaly that might [NOT] prevent complete insertion of the electrode array.
  3. Unrealistic expectations on the part of the candidate [AND] [OR] candidate's family, regarding the possible benefits, risks, [AND] limitations that are inherent to the surgical procedure(s) [AND] prosthetic devices.
  4. Unwillingness [OR] [NOT] ability of the candidate to comply with all investigational requirements.
  5. Active middle ear infection.
  6. Tinnitus primary motivation for implantation.
